      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Ab initio molecular dynamics made first-principles simulations of atomic motion practical, bridging electronic structure and real materials behavior. Its methodological reach across physics and chemistry is exceptional.",
        "attribution": "Car and Parrinello are appropriately credited as co-inventors of the method.",
        "maturity": "Decades of use and development establish its lasting scientific impact.",
        "uncertainties": ["The Nobel case depends on judging a computational method as a discovery of comparable stature to a specific physical phenomenon."]
      }
